tonight we're remembering the sacrifices  made by americans on 9 11. sandy  bradshaw was a flight attendant on  united flight 93 the hijacked plane that  went down in pennsylvania to remember  her her mother attends the memorial in  her hometown every year melissa painter  from our sister station brings us the  story of what it means that the  community continues to honor her  daughter's legacy  my mother called me and  said do you have your tv on and i said  no and she said well turn it on some  plane crashed into a building in new  york most of us of a certain age have  strong memories of september 11 2001.  most of us though don't have a daughter  who died on one of the hijacked planes  i'm sure that she was that she did her  part because that was the person she was  pat wah is the mother of sandy bradshaw  bradshaw was a flight attendant on  united airlines flight 93  bradshaw and others on board thwarted  the terrorist plans instead the plane  crashed into a field in shanksville  pennsylvania killing all on board 20  years later wa's home is decorated with  mementos that remind her of her daughter  and what happened that day that's always  helped me  to talk about it but  i struggled for a long time  and she still struggles but keeping the  legacy of her brave daughter alive helps  most years she attends a 9 11 ceremony  at eastern randolph high school where  her daughter graduated in 1981. that  annual ceremony also recognizes first  responders who serve our community wall  says it's a reminder to the generation  not even born in 2001 that the  sacrifices of that day continue on i  hope that people will remember  9 11 not i mean not just because of  sandy but because of what it was and  you know our our world changed that day  not just ours personally but  our whole world changed and it's never  been the same since we must never forget  that was melissa painer reporting
 

